  m_text: True ribs, or vertebrocostal ribs, are the first seven pairs of ribs that
    directly articulate anteriorly with the sternum via their own costal cartilages.
    These ribs are numbered 1 to 7 and are more fixed in position compared to the
    lower ribs. Owing to this direct sternal connection, true ribs provide essential
    protection to the thoracic organs, including the heart and lungs. Their design
    allows for an effective expansion and contraction of the thoracic cage during
    respiration. Any deformation or injury to these ribs may have implications on
    respiratory function and thoracic protection.
  m_isRightToLeft: 0
