  m_text: "The pubis, or pubic bone, is one of the three primary bones that make
    up the pelvis. Located anteriorly, it joins in the midline with the pubis of
    the opposite side, forming the pubic symphysis\u2014a cartilaginous joint. The
    pubis plays a crucial role in supporting and protecting internal reproductive
    organs and assists in bearing the body's weight in the seated position. Its superior
    edge provides attachment for abdominal muscles, while its posterior portion articulates
    with the ilium and ischium, completing the pelvic ring. The pubis is essential
    for stability, weight-bearing, and contributes to the birthing canal in females."
  m_isRightToLeft: 0
  m_fontAsset: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 8f586378b4e144a9851e7b34d9b748ee, type: 2}
