      m_Calls: []
  m_text: The left lacrimal bone is a small, thin bone located in the medial wall
    of the eye socket (orbit). It sits between the frontal process of the maxilla
    and the lamina papyracea of the ethmoid bone. The bone has a groove, the lacrimal
    groove, which, combined with the lacrimal sulcus of the maxilla, forms the nasolacrimal
    canal. This canal houses the nasolacrimal duct, responsible for draining tears
    from the eye to the nasal cavity. Due to its delicate nature, the lacrimal bone
    is vulnerable to fractures in orbital traumas.
  m_isRightToLeft: 0
  m_fontAsset: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 8f586378b4e144a9851e7b34d9b748ee, type: 2}
  m_sharedMaterial: {fileID: 2180264, guid: 8f586378b4e144a9851e7b34d9b748ee, type: 2}
