      m_Calls: []
  m_text: The left fibula is the slender and lateral bone of the lower leg, situated
    alongside the more robust tibia. While it does not bear significant weight like
    the tibia, it plays a crucial role in stabilizing the ankle and providing attachment
    sites for various muscles. Proximally, it connects with the tibia below the knee
    and distally, it forms the lateral malleolus, a prominent structure on the outer
    aspect of the ankle. The fibula's position and slender nature make it vulnerable
    to fractures, especially from lateral blows. Additionally, a segment of the fibula
    can be used for grafting procedures due to its relatively non-weight-bearing
    function.
  m_isRightToLeft: 0
