      m_Calls: []
  m_text: 'The lumbar vertebrae constitute the lower back segment of the vertebral
    column, located between the thoracic vertebrae and the sacrum. In humans, there
    are typically five lumbar vertebrae, labeled L1 through L5. Key features of the
    lumbar vertebrae include:

    Vertebral Body: These are the largest and strongest
    vertebral bodies in the spine.

    Spinous Processes: Broad and rectangular
    in shape, these processes project directly backward and are palpable under the
    skin.

    Transverse Processes: These protrude laterally from the junction of
    the pedicles and laminae.

    Articular Processes: Four in number for each vertebra.'
  m_isRightToLeft: 0
  m_fontAsset: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 8f586378b4e144a9851e7b34d9b748ee, type: 2}
