  m_text: The left patella, commonly known as the kneecap, is a small, triangular-shaped
    sesamoid bone that sits anteriorly within the tendon of the quadriceps femoris
    muscle. It articulates with the femoral trochlea, a groove on the femur, to form
    the patellofemoral joint. The patella functions to enhance leverage of the quadriceps
    tendon, thereby facilitating knee extension. It also provides protection to the
    knee joint. Being a frontline structure, the patella is susceptible to injuries
    such as fractures or dislocations, which can impair knee function and may require
    medical attention or intervention.
  m_isRightToLeft: 0
